Subject: local: run the agent sandboxes on CA-bearing images

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. Breadboard-local substitution, recorded under decision 3 of
the Fullsend integration conformance plan.

The sandbox supervisor builds its upstream TLS trust from the system bundle
when it starts. The conformance forge is served by a cert-manager CA that
exists only in this cluster, so without that CA present before the supervisor
starts, every proxied HTTPS request to the forge fails its handshake and the
agent sees a connection reset. Uploading a CA afterwards does not help: the
roots are read once.

The OpenShell chart at the deployed version exposes no way to inject a CA into
sandbox pods, so the CA has to be in the image.

Two images need it, because the harnesses do not share one. Triage runs on
fullsend-sandbox; review and code both pin the same fullsend-code digest, so
one local build covers both, and all three harnesses are substituted here. Each local image is built FROM the exact digest
the harness pins, adding only ca-certificates and the cluster CA — that image
plus one recorded layer, not a substitute assembled elsewhere.

deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh reads each base digest out of the
harness file that pins it rather than repeating it, so a harness that moves to
a new image stops the build instead of quietly producing a local image on a
stale base. It also fails rather than shipping an image whose trust store is
wrong. See deploy/fullsend-sandbox-local/Containerfile, which takes the base
repository as a build argument and is shared by both.

Drop this patch if the chart gains sandbox CA injection, or if the forge is
ever served by a publicly trusted certificate.

Breadboard note: applied to the agents mirror by
deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-upstream-agents.py.

